  "notes": "CONJUGATION (ichidan):\n- Negative: ぶれない\n- Te-form: ぶれて\n- Past: ぶれた\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive.\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 1 is common in photography. Sense 2 is widely used in business, politics, and everyday conversation to describe inconsistency or lack of a firm stance. ぶれない (unwavering) is often used as praise.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {手|て}ぶれ: camera shake (noun form)\n- {写真|しゃしん}がぶれる: photo is blurry\n- {軸|じく}がぶれない: unwavering in one's principles\n- {方針|ほうしん}がぶれる: policy wavers",
